  title: "Bridge to Terabithia", author: "Katherine Paterson", genre: "Literature", aliases: ["terabithia"],
  note: "A main character dies in this book. Preview the second half before reading it with students.",
  summary: "Jess Aarons, a fifth grader in rural Virginia, has trained all summer to be the fastest runner in his grade, but a new girl, Leslie Burke, beats everyone. Jess and Leslie become best friends and create Terabithia, a secret kingdom in the woods that they reach by swinging across a creek on a rope. Together they face bullies at school, and Leslie helps Jess believe in his art and imagination. One day Jess goes on a trip to an art museum in Washington with his music teacher, and while he is gone, Leslie tries to cross the flooded creek alone and drowns. Jess struggles with grief and guilt, then builds a real bridge to Terabithia and brings his little sister May Belle there as its new queen.",
  somebody_wanted_but_so_then: "Jess wanted to be special and to have a true friend, but his life felt small until Leslie arrived, so they created Terabithia together, then after Leslie died, Jess carried on her gift of imagination by sharing Terabithia with May Belle.",
