  note: null,
  summary: "Anna and her little brother Caleb live on the prairie with their father, Papa. Their mother died the day after Caleb was born, and the house has been quiet and lonely. Papa puts an advertisement in the newspaper for a wife, and Sarah Wheaton from Maine writes back and comes to stay for a month. Sarah brings her cat, Seal, and shells and stories from the sea she misses. The children grow to love her and fear she will leave. Sarah learns to drive the wagon, and one day she goes to town alone, and the children worry. She comes back with colored pencils in the colors of the sea and says she will stay.",
