  note: "Includes the death of Esperanza's father and scenes of hardship. Preview before discussing.",
  summary: "Esperanza Ortega lives a rich life on her family's ranch in Aguascalientes, Mexico. Just before her thirteenth birthday, her father is killed by bandits, and her uncle burns their home when her mother refuses to marry him. Esperanza and her mother escape to California with their former servants, Hortensia, Alfonso, and their son Miguel. They live in a camp for farm workers during the Great Depression. Esperanza must learn to work hard for the first time. When Mama becomes very sick, Esperanza takes care of the family and saves money to bring her grandmother, Abuelita, to California. In the end, Esperanza learns to be grateful and hopeful again.",
